Local adaptation: WatchDot, 2026-11-04.
App branding, personal signing configuration, spoken-reply controls and installation documentation were modified locally. Original attribution and license are retained.

Standalone Watch adaptation and public-source preparation: 2026-11-09.
The application was adapted to device-code authorization, CallKit-owned audio,
independent ICE-TCP media, a Watch-only interface and a WidgetKit face launcher.
The public package removes the obsolete iPhone app and app-owned Bluetooth/UDP
transports, local research/client artifacts, account/device diagnostics and caches.
The original Watch Dot attribution and GPL-3.0-only license are retained.

The native audio implementation contains OpenClaw-derived code and uses str0m
and libopus. Their copyright and license notices are preserved in
src/Vendor/Notices; the locked component inventory is INDEX.json in that folder.
Native wrapper/engine sources and the libopus source distribution are included
under src/Native. The device-code flow follows the public Codex protocol as a
protocol reference; this is not an assertion of endorsement by OpenAI.

The app icon is the WatchDot project artwork. The distributed waiting sound is
originally generated from mathematical oscillators by scripts/generate_ringback.py.
No sound extracted from ChatGPT, desktop ASAR contents, decompilation output or
personal account/signing material is part of this public package.
